---
import LatexLogo from '../components/LatexLogo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LogicTool from '../components/LogicTool.svelte';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={'Truth tables | lab by faris0x'}
  description="Build exact truth tables for propositional formulas, classify them as tautologies or contradictions, and export the table as a .tex file."
  current="logic"
  math
>
  <div class="tool-head">
    <div>
      <h1>Truth tables</h1>
    </div>
    <p>
      Enter a propositional formula and see every row. Each subformula gets its
      own column, and the finished table exports as <LatexLogo /> for your notes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <LogicTool client:idle />

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reading">
    <h2 id="reading">Reading the table</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The first columns list every assignment of truth values to the
      propositional variables. The remaining columns evaluate each distinct
      subformula from the inside out; the last column is the whole formula.
    </p>
    <p class="section-intro">
      A formula with a true final column in every row is a tautology. One with
      a false final column in every row is a contradiction. Anything else is
      contingent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="syntax">
    <h2 id="syntax">Syntax</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list section-intro">
      <li><strong>Negation</strong>: <code>~p</code> or <code>!p</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Conjunction</strong>: <code>p &amp; q</code> or <code>p ^ q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Disjunction</strong>: <code>p | q</code> or <code>p v q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Implication</strong>: <code>p -&gt; q</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Equivalence</strong>: <code>p &lt;-&gt; q</code>.</li>
      <li>Use parentheses to group; <code>~</code> binds tightest, then <code>&amp;</code>, <code>|</code>, <code>-&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;-&gt;</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="export">
    <h2 id="export">Export</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The <LatexLogo /> tab previews the document and lets you copy or download
      the <code>.tex</code> source. It uses <code>amsmath</code>,
      <code>amssymb</code> and <code>array</code>, so a standard TeX
      installation compiles the table.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
